1
00:00:00,244 --> 00:00:04,500
An Account represents an organization, a Contact a person, and

2
00:00:04,510 --> 00:00:06,755
an Opportunity a potential sale.

3
00:00:07,074 --> 00:00:09,062
Objects organize types of records;

4
00:00:09,471 --> 00:00:11,226
fields store their attributes.

5
00:00:11,520 --> 00:00:15,528
Relationships connect those pieces so the system can represent the

6
00:00:15,528 --> 00:00:16,819
business accurately.

7
00:00:17,861 --> 00:00:22,452
Atlantic Technology hires fictional Bright Media to manage its campaign.

8
00:00:22,771 --> 00:00:27,346
The advertiser, agency, creative approver, and payer may be different

9
00:00:27,346 --> 00:00:28,057
parties.

10
00:00:28,377 --> 00:00:33,186
A single free-text customer field cannot reliably capture every relationship

11
00:00:33,196 --> 00:00:34,436
or responsibility.

12
00:00:35,514 --> 00:00:40,645
Salesforce’s advertising sales data model includes specialized concepts around products,

13
00:00:40,999 --> 00:00:44,242
targeting, media plans, quotes, and orders.

14
00:00:44,583 --> 00:00:49,637
Available features depend on the software edition, licensing, and configuration.

15
00:00:49,953 --> 00:00:54,060
The diagrams here explain concepts rather than expose Axios’s private

16
00:00:54,060 --> 00:00:54,803
screens.

17
00:00:55,842 --> 00:01:00,420
Michael may need negotiation details while Olivia needs delivery readiness.

18
00:01:00,752 --> 00:01:04,389
Page layouts and Lightning pages can organize what they see.

19
00:01:04,721 --> 00:01:08,732
Before adding another field, check whether the information already exists

20
00:01:08,755 --> 00:01:10,548
and where it properly belongs.

21
00:01:11,560 --> 00:01:14,830
Removing a field from a page layout does not establish

22
00:01:14,854 --> 00:01:16,406
underlying data security.

23
00:01:16,742 --> 00:01:21,521
Access also depends on object permissions, field-level security, and record

24
00:01:21,521 --> 00:01:22,096
sharing.

25
00:01:22,406 --> 00:01:26,065
Use the relevant access controls and test the actual user

26
00:01:26,065 --> 00:01:26,979
experience.

27
00:01:28,026 --> 00:01:32,189
If Michael needs one shared account, investigate that need and

28
00:01:32,189 --> 00:01:32,977
its approval.

29
00:01:33,297 --> 00:01:36,173
Broad access to everything is not the default fix.

30
00:01:36,506 --> 00:01:40,323
Least privilege means providing the capabilities required for the work,

31
00:01:40,462 --> 00:01:43,171
with appropriate authorization and oversight.
